    "extracted text": "The paper discusses two main aluminum alloys: Al-0.09Sc-0.045Zr at.% (Alloy 1) and Al-0.06Sc-0.03Zr at.% (Alloy 2). These alloys were developed for non-quenchable aluminum metal matrix composites. The paper also examines Al-MMCs with Saffil (alumina) short fibers at volume fractions of 0%, 4%, and 15%. The alloys were subjected to a two-step aging treatment: 300°C for 4h followed by 425°C for 8h. The alloys show precipitation strengthening through formation of Al3(Sc,Zr) nano-precipitates. The paper compares these alloys with commercial alloys like AA5083-H131 and AA6061-T6 for armor applications.",
